==English==
{{wikipedia}}
[[Image:Bouguereau-The First Mourning-1888.jpg|thumb|William Adolphe Bouguereau's ''The First Mourning'' (1888)]]

===Etymology===
From {{inh|en|enm|Abel}}, from {{inh|en|ang|Ābel}}, from {{der|en|la|Abel}}, from {{der|en|grc|Ἅβελ}}, from {{der|en|hbo|הֶבֶל||Abel|tr=Héḇel}}, possibly from the homonymous word {{m|hbo|הֶבֶל||breath, vapor; vanity|tr=heḇel}} or from {{der|en|akk|𒌉𒍑|tr=ablu|t=son}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|en|/ˈeɪ.bl̩/}}
* {{homophones|en|able}}

===Proper noun===
{{en-proper noun}}

# {{senseid|en|Q313421}}{{lb|en|biblical character}} The son of [[Adam]] and [[Eve]] who was killed by his brother [[Cain]].
#* {{RQ:King James Version|Genesis|4|8|passage=And Cain talked with '''Abel''' his brother: and it came to pass, when they were in the field, that Cain rose up against '''Abel''' his brother, and slew him.}}
# {{given name|en|male|from=Hebrew}}.
# {{surname|en|from=patronymics}}.
# {{place|en|ucomm|co/Cleburne County|s/Alabama|c/USA}}, named after the biblical Abel.

